Let $[x]^k=x(x+1)\cdots(x+k-1)$, and let $p(\alpha)\propto[\alpha]^m/[c\alpha+a]^b$ on $\alpha>0$, with $m,b$ nonnegative integers, $b\ge m+2$ and $a,c>0$ (the Pochhammer prior). Let $
u=1+\mathbf{1}(m\ge1)$. Then $\int_0^\delta p\asymp\delta^{
u}$ as $\delta\downarrow0$. The Cesaro risk bound $R_N\le\varepsilon-N^{-1}\log\int_0^{\sqrt\varepsilon}p$ therefore reads $R_N\le\varepsilon+ rac{
u}{2N}\log rac1\varepsilon+O(N^{-1})$, minimized at $\varepsilon=
u/(2N)$ to give $R_N= rac{
u}{2}N^{-1}\log N\{1+o(1)\}$. Hence every $m$ attains the rate $N^{-1}\log N$, and $m=0$ gives the smaller constant, $1/2$ against $1$ for every $m\ge1$.
